From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rory Axton <roryaxton@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] 0919 redfin: camera sensors powered up, chip IDs read (sweetcam)

New bsd/dev/sweet_cam.c, after HackiOS redwood_camera.c (cam=1/2): the rear
IMX363, the rear ultra-wide IMX481 and the front IMX355 powered up in their
Android module files' order (SLG51000 LDOs over SE9 I2C at 0x75, PM8150L GPIO
2/8 for the front custom rail and the rear VAF regulator, reset GPIO 23/25/21,
MCLK0-2 from camcc at the crystal's 19.2 MHz, titan top GDSC), the chip ID
register 0x0016 read by hand on the CCI pins (17/18, 19/20, 27/28), powered
down again. The SLG51000 gets Google's slg51000_config_tuning() first.
sweetcam=1 looks, =2 probes on request (poke "c N", 9 = look), =3 probes all
three at boot; "c 10" reads the PMIC GPIOs, "c 11" the SLG51000 (r16a reset
during those reads at boot: now separate, each line given 300 ms to reach the
log). The GCC camera XO clock (off here, critical in Linux) is switched on.
sweet_haptic.c exports sweet_se9_xfer() for the PMIC.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WuzsiVGCDDmN2GPRLJvX3w
